# Model routing for the Ralph loop and for generated agent definitions.
# Edit here, then run `node scripts/sync-agents.mjs` so .claude/agents and .codex/agents pick it up.
#
# Tiers (Maxx, 2026-09-03):
#   worker   — implements one task per iteration        → GPT 5.6 Terra @ high   | Claude Sonnet 5 @ high
#   reviewer — reviews the diff against the spec        → GPT Sol 5.6   @ high   | Claude Opus 5  @ high
#   planner  — re-plans, updates specs/progress, DONE   → GPT Sol 5.6   @ xhigh  | Claude Opus 5  @ xhigh
#   auditor  — human-invoked final QA (not run by loop.sh) → GPT Sol 5.6   @ xhigh  | Claude Fable 5.1 / Opus 5 @ xhigh
# Both columns are complete routings; mixing vendors across tiers is fine. Keep the constitution's Roles table in step.
#
# RUNNER selects which CLI the loop drives: "claude" or "codex".
RUNNER=${RUNNER:-claude}

# ---- Claude Code (aliases sonnet/opus resolve to the current Claude 5 family; full IDs also accepted) ----
CLAUDE_WORKER_MODEL=sonnet
CLAUDE_WORKER_EFFORT=high
CLAUDE_REVIEWER_MODEL=opus
CLAUDE_REVIEWER_EFFORT=high
CLAUDE_PLANNER_MODEL=opus
CLAUDE_PLANNER_EFFORT=xhigh

# ---- Codex CLI ----
# Verified 2026-09-03 with live Codex CLI calls on this account: `gpt-5.6-terra` accepts high and
# `gpt-5.6-sol` accepts high/xhigh. If a model later rejects xhigh, the loop falls back to high (see loop.sh).
CODEX_WORKER_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
CODEX_WORKER_EFFORT=high
CODEX_REVIEWER_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
CODEX_REVIEWER_EFFORT=high
CODEX_PLANNER_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
CODEX_PLANNER_EFFORT=xhigh

# ---- Loop guardrails ----
MAX_ITERATIONS=50          # hard stop per `ralph/loop.sh` invocation
MAX_TURNS_BUILD=80         # agentic turns per build step (claude --max-turns)
MAX_TURNS_REVIEW=30
MAX_TURNS_PLAN=40
